<title>USA: Vertex says gets U.S. patent for VX-835.</title>
<headline>Vertex says gets U.S. patent for VX-835.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vertex Pharmaceuticals Inc said on Monday that the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office issued the company a patent covering VX-853 and related compounds.</p>
<p>Vertex is developing VX-853 for the treatment of cancer multidrug resistance, which limits the efficacy of many cancer chemotherapy regimens.</p>
<p>In April Vertex began a Phase I/II dose-escalating clinical trial of VX-853 in combination with doxorubicin, a well-established chemotherapeutic agent.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1733</p>
